WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.930
It's Thursday, November 19, and this is the Transhuman Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.550
Let's catch you up on the last 24 hours in transhumanism.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.780
Remember this! In old mice,

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:21.410
Sydney scientists' nose drops brought memory back to youthful levels.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:27.680
And over 30 years, chronic loneliness came with a 38% higher dementia risk.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.610
Google's Genie 4, an AI that builds worlds you can walk through,

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.770
just opened to top-tier subscribers.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:41.640
A startup called Osmo claims its AI nose now

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.380
smells about as well as the average person.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.520
SimCity's creator Will Wright is building a g

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.160
ame that turns your memories into an AI world.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:56.730
And AIs briefly forget old skills while learning new ones.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:58.940
Researchers now ask if we do too.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.190
On to longevity.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:07.090
Biogen says its tau drug slowed early Alzheimer's decline by 38% at two years.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.480
And a review of 11 studies linked the cold

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:13.470
sore virus to a 48% higher dementia risk.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:15.820
In London,

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:21.890
a vest with 256 electrodes maps an ageing heart's wiring in five minutes.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.250
And in mice,

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:28.530
tiny particles from stem cells calmed the immune attack and delayed type 1 diabetes.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.940
On to wellbeing.

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:35.700
Young adults who cut back on social media saw their depression and anxiety ease.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.730
And in a small trial,

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:43.820
12 weeks of exercise before talk therapy for depression sharpened memory and learning.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.960
Now, the catch.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:51.420
US auditors talked four top chatbots past their safeguards into making attack plans.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:57.430
And Lilly's dopamine pill for Alzheimer's missed its goal in a 300-person trial.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:05.650
A soft robot with no electronics, printed in one piece,

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:08.260
now runs nearly five metres a second.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:10.000
Closer to home,

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:15.170
UNSW can check an old EV battery cell's health in under three minutes.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:20.700
And Voyager 1 just became the first spacecraft a full light-day from Earth,

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:22.600
nearly 50 years after launch.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:25.370
Cambridge Dictionary's word of the year?

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:28.140
Human. Whatever we build next, remember this.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.510
Zoom out, and the line only goes up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.950
Every day, the future shows up a little earlier.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.040
All of that, in one day. And the days keep getting bigger.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.170
You've been watching the Transhuman Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.350
Go build the future. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.600
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney on November 27.
